<x-layout title="Booking terms" description="Booking, payment, cancellation and weather terms for All Things Tobago tours and activities.">
    <section class="bg-ink text-white"><div class="wrap py-14"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Terms</p><h1 class="h-section mt-3">Booking terms, in plain words.</h1></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="wrap max-w-3xl prose-site">
        <p><strong>Requests and confirmation.</strong> A request on this site is not a confirmed booking until we reply to confirm availability. Prices shown are "from" prices in TTD and are confirmed in that reply. US$ figures are approximate.</p>
        <p><strong>Payment.</strong> Pay in cash (TTD or USD), by bank transfer, or by card through a payment link. Some boat trips and peak-season dates need a deposit to hold the spot; we tell you before you pay.</p>
        <p><strong>Cancellation.</strong> Cancel 48 hours or more before the start for a full refund of any deposit. Inside 48 hours deposits are kept, except where we cancel.</p>
        <p><strong>Weather and safety.</strong> Captains and guides make the final call on sea and road conditions. If we cancel, you choose a new date or a full refund of anything paid.</p>
        <p><strong>Your responsibilities.</strong> Tell us about non-swimmers, medical conditions, pregnancy and children's ages when booking. Follow crew instructions and wear the life jackets provided. Guests under the influence may be refused for safety without refund.</p>
        <p><strong>Third-party suppliers.</strong> Some experiences, stays and events are delivered by partner operators. We choose them carefully and remain your point of contact throughout.</p>
    </div></section>
</x-layout>
